- description: Experimental Actions queries, ABOM's own and upstream's

# Separate from `abom-findings.qls` so that what ABOM reports by default and what it reports to
# seed a corpus are two decisions. A finding from here carries an `abom/experimental/` rule id,
# which is what lets a consumer tell it from an upstream one and drop it.
#
# The point of the suite is coverage rather than security: a repository with no upstream findings
# produces nothing, and nothing is indistinguishable from a repository nobody analyzed. Seeding a
# marker per job gives the ingest, attribution and interface paths something real to carry without
# waiting for a corpus that happens to have problems in it.

# This pack's own queries. `.` is exact while every query here is experimental; a query that
# graduates into the default suite gets an explicit filter rather than a second pack.
- queries: .

# Upstream's experimental set. Precision is a property of the rule, and a consumer filtering on
# rule id can always drop these — whereas a finding never collected cannot be recovered.
#
# Pinned exactly rather than by range: without `version:` the CLI resolves the most recent pack,
# so the set of rules ABOM attributes could change with no commit here.
- queries: experimental
  from: codeql/actions-queries
  version: 0.6.35
